            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0812" n="684" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg684"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 521.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Reed to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-02-05"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 5, 1885</date>.
                        (Received February 24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 301.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 289, in
                    regard to the translation of manifests in Cuba and Porto Rico, I beg to inclose
                    a copy of my note to the minister of state upon the subject, dated the 8th
                    December, 1884. The minister replied on the 3d ultimo that the subject had been
                    referred to the minister of ultramar.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DWIGHT T. REED.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d521-a1.xml" xpointer="d521-a1"/>
